e('| runc | Creates the container, then exits |','| runc | OCI lifecycle CLI used by the shim |','Attachedruncommandcanremain.',[run])
e('Crucially, **runc exits once the container is running**. It is not a daemon. Alternatives implement the same interface: **crun** (written in C, smaller and faster to start), **runsc** (gVisor) and **kata-runtime** (lightweight VMs). Swapping them is a config change.','In the shim-managed create/start workflow, **runc lifecycle commands return** and the shim supervises the running process. An attached runc run invocation can remain until the workload exits. Alternatives such as crun, gVisor runsc and Kata provide different implementations or isolation models; compatibility and runtime integration must be checked before switching.','runcattachedmodecontradicts always exits;unverifiedspeedrankingremoved.',[run,sh])
e('For each container it starts a **shim** process, which then calls runc. The shim becomes the container\'s parent: it keeps stdin/stdout open, reaps the process and records its exit status.','A **shim** supervises tasks and separates their lifetime from the containerd daemon. The runc-v2 shim can group multiple containers, for example a Kubernetes pod, and manages I/O and exit reporting.','Currentruntimev2grouping.',[sh])
e('Because of the shim, you can **restart containerd or dockerd without killing running containers**. They are children of shims, not of the daemon. Upgrading the container daemon on a busy node does not restart its workloads.','The shim design allows tasks to survive a containerd daemon restart if shims/tasks are preserved and reconnection remains compatible. Service-manager stop behavior and upgrade compatibility still matter. Docker daemon shutdown normally stops containers unless supported **live restore** is enabled; live restore also has documented limitations.','Dangerousdockerdrestartalwayssurvivesfalse.',[sh,lr])
e('because they are OCI images.','because supported Docker/OCI image formats remain compatible.','DockerimagesnotalwaysstrictOCImediatypes.',[cri])
e('Each `RUN`, `COPY` and `ADD` produces a new file system layer;','`RUN`, `COPY` and `ADD` can produce filesystem changesets; empty results and build optimisations affect exported layers.','Notliteraloneexportedlayeralways.',[df])
e('BuildKit (Docker\'s builder since 23.0)','BuildKit (the default Docker builder for Linux images since Engine 23.0)','Windowsbuilderexception.',[bk])
e('- For `RUN`, the input is the **command string** and the parent layer. It does not look at what the command would fetch.','- For a simple RUN, the command, parent state and relevant build configuration matter; mounts and build arguments can add inputs. Cache lookup does not execute the command to discover changed remote content.','Cachekeynotonlystringparent.',[c])
e('not their timestamps.','with modification time specifically excluded from the cache checksum.','Metadata includesmorethancontent;notalltimestampgeneralization.',[c])
e('**Once a step misses, every later step re-runs**, since each layer\'s parent has changed.','**Dependent steps may lose cache reuse** when their inputs change. This explains a simple sequential stage; BuildKit can cache independent stages or linked COPY operations separately.','DAG/linkcacheexception.',[bk,df])
e('Editing `app.py` changes only the final `COPY . .`,','Assuming the base image, builder configuration and other inputs stay fixed, editing `app.py` changes the final `COPY . .`,','Mutablebasecaninvalidatecache.',[c])
e('is cached for ever,','can be reused from cache despite changed repositories,','Cachecanprune/expire/inputchange.',[c])
e('Every layer is permanent.','Published immutable layer content remains part of images that reference it; unreferenced blobs can be garbage-collected.','Permanentnotliterallyforever.',[l])
e('```\nRUN curl -o big.tgz $URL # +300 MB','The following illustrates uncompressed file bytes and ignores metadata/compression:\n\n```\nRUN curl -o big.tgz $URL # +300 MB','Wirecompressedimagenotrawsum.',[l])
e('FROM golang:1.23 AS build','FROM golang:1 AS build','OldspecificGo exampleversionstalenotnecessary;movabletagclearlyillustrative.',[df])
e('The final image contains a static binary and almost nothing else: perhaps 10–20 MB instead of nearly 1 GB, with far fewer packages for vulnerability scanners to flag.','For a compatible Go project, this copies only the built binary into the final base. CGO_ENABLED=0 does not make every project buildable or eliminate runtime data dependencies. Distroless provides selected runtime files but not a general shell/package-manager environment. Image size and vulnerability exposure must be measured; no fixed size reduction is asserted.', 'Removeunsupportedsizeandsecurityequivalence;CGOcompatibility.', ['https://github.com/GoogleContainerTools/distroless',df])
e('provides credentials that never end up in the image.','temporarily exposes credentials without automatically persisting the mount. A build command can still copy secrets into layers or print them to logs, so handling matters.','Secretmountnotpreventsdeliberatecopy/log.',[sec])
